    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it says \"the consensus remains divided\" but i feel like reading a lot of these journals, there seems to be a much stronger argument that the growth part was actually the primary outcome while the inequality stuff is just a side effect or a result of other things. isn't it generally accepted that the deregulation was the main driver for the growth we saw after that?",
