    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While some scholarly arguments lean strongly toward deregulation being the primary driver of post-1980s growth, stating it is \"generally accepted\" would be an oversimplification of academic discourse. Most economists acknowledge that deregulation was a significant contributing factor, but few agree it was the *sole* or *primary* driver in isolation. The growth observed is often attributed to a complex interplay of multiple factors, including technological advancements and globalization as well.",
      "source": "target",
