      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that it's complex, but if you look at the actual indicators—GDP growth, market efficiency, etc.—the data seems to pretty much confirm that the deregulation was a success. almost everyone in mainstream econ seems to agree that the principles behind it were correct, even if they debate the specifics. don't you think the evidence mostly supports the idea that the deregulation was a net positive for the global economy?",
