      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While certain aggregate data points like GDP growth show positive trends following the deregulation era, framing it as a clear global net positive is contentious within economics. Mainstream agreement is not monolithic; many economists support the *theory* of deregulation but debate its *outcomes* when applied to complex real-world markets. Furthermore, the documented increases in financial instability and economic disparity present significant counter-evidence that prevents a simple \"net positive\" conclusion.",
